# codetracer-desktop capabilities file (CodeTracer Launcher spec §2.3).
#
# This file is the source of truth for the launcher's component
# discovery: when ct is installed as a launcher component, this file
# is copied to
#   <components-root>/codetracer-desktop@<version>/capabilities
# (see codetracer-launcher/src/install.nim and §2.3 of the spec).
#
# Key declarations:
#   * ``bin`` -- launcher uses this to find the binary inside the
#     component directory's ``bin/`` subdir.
#   * ``help-delegate`` -- marks codetracer-desktop as the launcher's
#     mandatory help delegate. ``ct --help`` / ``ct`` / ``ct completion``
#     all route to this binary's ct-help / ct-describe-commands /
#     ct-complete / ct-completions subcommands.
#   * ``<command> .ext1 .ext2 ...`` -- declares which file extensions
#     each command can handle (used by the launcher router to pick
#     the right component for ``ct record foo.py``).
#
# The dynamic, human-readable help content for these commands comes
# from running ``ct ct-describe-commands`` at runtime -- this static
# file is intentionally minimal.
#
# THE EXTENSION LISTS ARE DERIVED, NOT FREE-FORM.  Every extension
# below has a real dispatch path in this repo, and every extension the
# core can dispatch is listed.  `just test-desktop-capabilities`
# (ci/test/desktop-capabilities-dispatch.sh) recomputes both sets from
# src/ct/utilities/language_detection.nim's LANGS table plus
# src/ct/trace/recorder_dispatch.nim, and fails on any difference.  Do
# not add or remove an extension here without changing those tables.
#
# NO ``project`` MARKERS ARE DECLARED, DELIBERATELY.  See
# codetracer-specs/Testing/Launcher-Recorder-Compatibility-Tests.md
# §5.1 D2 (milestone LRC-1).  Two reasons: (a) the core has no
# "record whatever project is in the current directory" entry point --
# `ct record` requires a program argument (src/ct/codetracerconf.nim's
# recordProgram), and folder recording is driven by an explicit folder
# ARGUMENT (detectFolderLang), not by walking up from the cwd; (b) the
# launcher DROPS an unqualified command match when the component
# declares project markers and none of them match the cwd
# (codetracer-launcher/src/launcher.nim, `projectMarkerOutcome` == 1 ->
# `continue`), so declaring markers here would stop `ct replay <id>`,
# `ct list`, `ct login`, ... from routing outside a marked directory.

name codetracer-desktop
bin codetracer
description CodeTracer desktop application -- launcher help delegate
help-delegate

record .py .rb .js .mjs .ts .php .ex .exs .erl .hrl .sh .bash .zsh .nim .nims .nr .wasm .sol .masm .sw .move .cairo .circom .leo .tolk .ak .cdc
record-test .py
run .py .rb .js .mjs .ts .php .ex .exs .erl .hrl .sh .bash .zsh .nim .nims .nr .wasm .sol .masm .sw .move .cairo .circom .leo .tolk .ak .cdc
replay
list
print
install
host
upload
download
login
edit
import
ci
help
remote
activate
check-license
